          "question": "I get migraines maybe six times a month.",
          "answer": "Thanks for sharing. You said you get migraines about six times a month. I can explain what that frequency means, how it is classified, or what management and lifestyle options the guidance describes. I can also cover how it is coded in ICD-10, the international disease classification system.\n\nWhat would you like to know? For example:\n- What \"six times a month\" means in terms of how migraines are grouped\n- Lifestyle options such as diet, activity, or sleep\n- How treatment is generally approached\n- How the condition is classified\n\nIf any of your headaches feel different from your usual pattern, or are getting worse, a doctor who can examine you should assess them.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
